I shall be extremely interested to see how you (i.e. IBM) tackle
the multiple mode, interrupt and security problems that I have been
referring to.  I suspect that you will follow the well-threaded -
sorry, well-trodden - path that goes as follows:

    Introduce thread-level parallelism and a set of programming
rules to ensure that it works.
    Receive a flood of claims that the system is broken from people
not following the rules, but who think that they are.
    Attempt to kludge this up by education, operating system and
compiler hacking and so on.
    Eventually back off and impose a set of restrictions that
reduces the problem to one that is practically soluble.

Alternatively, the last might take the modern approach of saying
that it is all the users' fault, and unexplained crashes are just
something that systems have.


