I'm not sure I agree here - I would rather argue that pageable 
page tables are a misfeature that introduces way more drawbacks than
it solves in the first place and that the way to go is discardable
page tables. Page tables would not contain any persistent information
and would be discarded instead of being swaped out and regenerated instead
of being swaped in. One such present system is for example FreeBSD.

Regenration is bound to get cheaper and cheaper compared to swapping
over time aswell...

