I do not know anything about JFS.  Historically, MSFS started as a
research project by the DECwest engineerng group in Washington State. 
Its original goal was to be file system that would run on OpenVMS,
Windows-NT, and Digital UNIX.  However, only Digial UNIX was
interested.  The MSFS bits were then renamed to AdvFS when they were
integrated into the Digital UNIX kernel.

I was not there at the beginning, so I do not know what previous
research papers or file system examples helped influence the DECwest
engineers.  But I'm fairly sure that all the code was written from
scratch by Digital Equipment Corportion engineers (there are only
Digital (now Compaq) copyright notices in the source code; and code we
license from other sources does include the other sources copyright in
the source itself).

