The DECstation was one of OSF's reference platforms (i.e. one of the
platforms OSF did the port to).  If you go back to old gcc logs,
you'll find a ton of work done on gcc for MIPS/DECstation by Michael
Meissner for the OSF, because the OSF was using gcc and a new object
format (ROSE, which DEC discarded), and the DECstation was one of
their reference platforms (later gcc Changelogs have lots more from
Michael Meissner, since Cygnus Support hired him after the OSF got out
of the OS business).
