A large differentiator for Tru64 UNIX is clustering.
No vendor out there can do what we do, some may claim to but its all
smoke and mirrors.
We have an OS that is easy to manage, highly reliable and scalable.
We will continue to add features that will differentiate us in the
market.
AIX runs on IA-64 but IBM will always push their risc platform so how
comitted are they?
SUN may port Solaris but based on their commitment to the IA-32 version
it will likely be a half hearted attempt.
Tru64 will be the only UNIX committed to bringing all the features and
functions of a proprietary OS to a mainstream platform.
I would expect to see an early an early adoption program being brought
about so ISVs can be brought aboard quickly.
Tru64 UNIX may not conquer the world but we will aim to be number 1 or 2
in our target markets and we have already been very successful in doing
so.
There are several reports showing our excellent growth and increase in
market share.
Tru64 UNIX is a great product and it will continue to be so long into
the future.

btw LVM and advfs are unrelated.
LVM (logical volume manager) was the predecessor to LSM (though LSM is
not based on LVM).

Nick








