The code base for AdvFS was not based on the Berkely Fast File System
(which happens to be what the Tru64 UNIX UFS file system is).

I live and breath the AdvFS code base and I have from time to time
wondered into the UFS code base, and trust me when I say they are
nothing alike.  

They also have totally different on-disk metadata, and tons of other
differences.

The only thing they share is that from an application programs view,
they both provide the same file services, but under the covers, they do
it in totally different ways.

From an administrators view they have vastly different management
capabilities (I will not try to argue which are better, just that they
are different).

                                        Bob Harris


