"Aaron G. Sword" wrote:

> Greetings, does anyone know how to go about getting around the 8
> character restriction on usernames (and passwords for that matter) on
> Tru64 systems?  I am running v5.0a with shadow passwords.  Any help at
> all would be greatly appreciated.  Thanks ..

Passwords under the "shadow passwords" option can be up to 80 characters,
although I believe they default to 8 characters.  Check out the prpasswd
man page and the u_minlen and u_minchosen.  You should be able to modify
your /etc/auth/system/default file and add/modify the values in their to
suit your needs. When running shadow passwords you are essentially running
a very much so trimmed down enhanced security (eg. C2) environment.  As
you find need to add features to your security environment to take
advantage of some of "c2 functionality", all you need to do is enable
them.

Usernames are a different story though. Due to interoperability concerns
and "presentation" concerns increasing usernames from 8 characters to a
larger value has been an ongoing project.  There is a capability in the
v5.1 systems to have 64 character usernames; however, the tools to manage
and display longer usernames are still being modified, so full support for
longer names won't be available until some release after 5.1a.  There's a
system cell (man sysconf, grep for _SC_LOGIN_NAME_MAX) that will be used
to provide the functionality....

--

