Although Linux was never designed to be portable, it has turned out to be
highly portable.  And many of the microkernel architectures which were
very portable are only really used on one platform.  Microsoft put
immense effort into building a platform-free HAL microkernel, and they've
dumped all the platforms it supported except x86 (and now IA64).

Sometimes, what you design for and what actually gets done are two very
different things.

Dave


