> # ./Makefile
> ./Makefile: syntax error at line 22: `LIBTOOL=$' unexpected

Why are you trying to run the Makefile?  It's not a script, it's (essentially)
a configuration file used by the `make' command to explain how to build the
software.

You want to run the `make' command, not the Makefile, so try run just

	make

from the same directory containing the Makefile.

Also, there are all kinds of good reasons to never build software as root.
Compile the software as yourself, and then when you want to install it,
switch to root to do the

	make install

Tim
