Pull the controller out of the StorageWorks cabinet and look at the bottom
for the part number.  If it is 70-31490-01, the switches set the base SCSI
address for the drives in the cabinet.  Since a wide configuration supports
16 addresses, you can have your 7 StorageWorks slots appear at an arbitrary
starting address.  Count binary from the first switch designated (1) of the
7 total.

