> any doc/more help available on this.  I have only 1 tru64 machine.  Any
> alternate methods of carrying out remote debugging with say a linux
> machine  ??

dbx(1) is the standard kernel debugging tool (soon, ladebug(1) will work
well on kernels too).  The unsupported command "crash" is available off
the web and is considerably more powerful than dbx, IMHO.  Internally,
this tool is heavily used.

The nice thing about dbx -remote is that you can debug (set breakpoints,
etc.) on a running kernel at the SOURCE code level - NICE. It does
require 2 machines.  If you have only one machine or if you hae no
source access, I suggest using the "integrated kernel debugger" - see
the ikdebug(8) man page.

