You've got it a bit wrong. The syntax is:

<interface> <IP> <netmask> <action>

tu1 10.2.2.136 255.255.255.255 deny

And you don't have to reboot, a simple "ifconfig tu1 filter" will do it.
Actually, I don't think that any boot scripts call filtering... So, a reboot
will CLEAR any filters you set up, unless you put something in
/etc/inet.local

Nix.




