Daniel Grambihler wrote:
> 
> I'm having periodic problems with a PC164LX 533. It tends to crash
> when
> disk space runs low or virtual memory fills. I'm not sure which. I
> have no
> idea how to analyze the tru64 crash dumps, so if anyone could help,
> I'd
> really appreciate it. 

A machine check is TYPICALLY generated by a hardware failure (rarely
less than perfect kernel code can do it  too - but you didn't hear that
from me :-).  In this case it looks like the code was attempting to read
a register on your psiop card when the system went down.  The machine
check type is "670" which means a hard failure.

I'm not in the I/O group but I understand that this card is rather old
and that it has not been qualified on all platforms - aparently there
are some timing issues.  May I assume that you did not get this card
thru "official" channels?

Tony V.
Kernel Group


