A single read error.  Probably just a bad block.  Since this is a
SCSI disk you can use scu(8) to send a "reassign LBA" command to
the disk.  If it supports it, that will at least replace the bad
block with a good one.  It should try pretty hard to get good
data, but don't count on it.
