>verify: unable to get info for file <//sbin/rc2.d/K52write>; [5] I/O error
>
Since the problem touches a bunch of files, the block probably contains
metadata.  The AdvFS admin. guide may have suggestions for how to
handle the problem.  It is on the Associated Product CDROM that has
the AdvFS Utilities. 
>
>
>My question is if there is anything I can do to correct this error or do I
>have to replace the disk and do a restore from backup.

A single bad block, is usually not enough of a problem to warrant
replacing the whole disk.  You can use scu(8) command "verify" or
dd(1) to look for more bad blocks.  If that's the only one, replace
it and start fixing the file system.

