Not that I'm aware of, but I seem to remember seeing a message somewhere about
NIS+ on Linux -- it's possible there's some OpenSource widget available that
would give you what you need.

It took years and years for Sun to get buy-in from any other vendor (HP was
the first, IBM the second) for NIS+.  Although Sun will probably support NIS+
until Solaris 25.x (the next release, using Sun's numbering conventions ;-) ),
I've heard several rumors that even Sun is going to be moving away from NIS+
and moving to something more widely supported -- Kerberos & LDAP most likely.

NIS+ was an improvement over NIS, but it may never really get its day in the
Sun ;-)  If you get a chance, start investigating Kerberos & LDAP.  It's not
as easy out of the box as NIS+, but it *is* easily multiplatform, whereas
NIS+ is not.

Good luck,

