That depends on how comfortable you (and upper management) are "rolling
your own" solution in some areas.  My recommendation would be OpenLDAP,
but politics or other reasons may make you look at other implementations.

Depending on your timeframe, you may have to assemble some of the peices
that hook everything together yourself.  I can tell you that a lot of
sites are looking at the same middleware and IAA (identification,
authentication, and authorization) issues you're going to be dealing with.
The longer you wait, the more help there will be from other admins that
have already "been there, done that", but waiting isn't always an option.

As far as where to run the server, you're asking on a Tru64 group so most
of the respondents will probably answer Tru64.  I personally prefer Tru64
to Solaris too, but in the case of an LDAP server, it really doesn't matter
much.  Plan to have a secondary/backup LDAP server as well.

