>> My PWS500au dual-boots between Linux and Tru64, which I am trying to learn
>> about.
>> 
>> Under Linux, a lot of Pyxis machine checks are echoed to the console, this
>> doesn't happen in Tru64 though.  Are these errors logged, and if they are,
>> where are they logged?

See Also: uerf(8), dia(8), binlogd(8) and the various commands
reference from those.  Machine checks and related hardware errors
are logged to the binary error log file.  On older systems, uerf(8)
can at least read the file even if it can't always interpret the
content.  Modern versions of DECevent (dia) may be able interpret
what uerf(8) can't.

There are include files lurking about that describe the basic content
of the file, so a simple error log filter is a feasible program
if you have license to do software development.  The guts of the
various events depend entirely on whatever subsystem writes them.

--
Alan Rollow				alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com



