One of our systems died this weekend and I'd appreciate any advice
that could be offered.

The xp1000-500, tru64 4.0f(I think) machine died without a known 
precipitating event and did not reboot.  >>>sho_dev did not list the 
primary drive (dka0).  Booting from the installation media (4.0d)
failed as well (WARNING: proc_type 0x8/sys_type 0x22 unknown
panic (cpu0): init_platform not implemented on this platform).
However, after attempting to boot from the CD, dka0 showed up
in >>>sho_dev.  The first attempt to boot to it failed with
failed to send READ CAPACITY to dka0.0.0.6.1 (repeated 3x) and
ch_open: failed scsi 1 6 0 0 0 0 0, dka0.0.0.6.1.  Ok ,it looks
like the drive is having some problems.  A second attempt to boot
was 90%+ successful, dying (unknown fault as I wasn't looking at 
the time) before completion.  Subsequently, dka0 was not seen.
(Time passes...) A later repetition of CD "boot" and boot
newly found dka0 was successful.  I recovered some important
shared info.  The machine stayed up about 2 hours and died
in a similar fashion.  It might have partially rebooted twice
before officially losing dka0 again.

I suspect I can get the system alive a few, but finite, more
times with the CD "preboot".  Does anyone have any suggestions
or pointers to documents on what would be the best way to
prepare/backup the system that would allow for transfer/rebuild
of the system on a new drive?  I have done os installations but
no builds or rebuilds of this magnitude.  I have access to 
storage space on other systems as well as a tape drive in
this system (although large tape writes probably wouldn't
finish before the system crashed again).

I have searched for information on 'failed to send READ CAPACITY"
and ch_open failures but found nothing of interest (although it
seems pretty clear what's happening).  Is this likely a problem
with electronics that might be recoverable without a full
drive replacement?

Is there anything to be inferred from the CD boot process apparently
waking up dka0?

Other info:
The primary drive is a Compaq BB00921B91 (3B05).
I tried some cable swapping type things but they didn't help and
  no other device had any problems so I don't think it's the controller.
This system is NOT the one in which a kzpca was recently installed
  (and I asked about in this forum) and was not involved in that at all.

Kirk




