>is there any way to clone a systemdisk?

Lots of ways, but some depend on the version of the operating
system being used.

>Before crashing another system: Is it possible with a command as
>following:
>
>dd if=/dev(rz0c of=/dev/rz3c bs=8192

I would fix the typo and use the raw devices instead of
buffered devices, if I were going to do it this way.
You could use a large transfer size, which may help
the performance of the copy.

This method has the disadvantage that it copies data not
being used.  For file systems with sufficiently low usage
and the page/swap space, this can add up.  Any fragmentation
or organizational problems will be copied as well.

The use of /dev/rz device names implies V4 or earlier, so
the oddities of doing this on V5 aren't relevant.

>Can be bootet from rz3c afterwards?

If the target hardware configuration is indeed the same, it
should work..

