Apart from the network speed connection that someone else mentioned,
have you considered
the possibility that the Unix box is attempting to do a reverse lookup
on the IP address
that the PC clients are coming from, and failing....

Clearly since they are from the private network, the external DNS PTR
lookups will fail. You
may have to add them into the UNIX box /etc/hosts, and make sure the
host lookup order
in /etc/svc.conf is "hosts=local,bind", or else run a DNS server on your
nox which knows about the
private  address space.

(By the way, this is almost a FAQ; people usually ask "why is telnet
from my PC taking so long?"

