>What would be the benefit of using raw devices (rrz0c e.g.)? Speed?

Mostly.  Last I looked (but it has been years), the I/O size that
is used by the buffered device was only 2 KB, regardless of the size
you specify with dd(1).  There's also bound to be a bit of extra
latency and CPU usage as the data is copied from buffer cache to
program buffer.
  
