I don't what this guy's problem is, but I'm suspect of the above information.

The fact that the TLZ10 is a narrow device does NOT force the other equipment
on the SCSI bus to also run in narrow mode.  The controller negotiates with
each device on the bus for transfer speed and transfer width.

On the other hand, if the TLZ10 is not qualified on the wide SCSI bus, then it
may be preventing other wide devices from even showing up on the bus.

